<title>USA: BMC Industries to buy back one mln shares.</title>
<headline>BMC Industries to buy back one mln shares.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>BMC Industries Inc said Monday its board of directors approved a plan to repurchase up to one million of its common shares on the open market or in negotiated transactions.</p>
<p>The company did not disclose an exact timeframe for the stock buyback program, but said market conditions will determine the timing and terms.</p>
<p>BMC Industries said it has about 27.5 million common shares outstanding.</p>
<p>The company makes aperture masks for color picture tubes used in television sets and computer monitors.</p>
<p>Its shares closed up 3/4 Monday at 26-7/8.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
